<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">1. Direct fix: 9.5mm or 12.5mm plasterboard mechanically fixed to ceiling joists. Fastest and cheapest, suitable for most domestic ceilings.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">2. MF (metal frame) suspended ceiling: galvanised steel framework suspended on hangers from the structural ceiling, with plasterboard fixed to the frame. Allows for services (M&amp;E, ventilation) to be run in the void, gives a perfectly flat finish.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">3. Lay-in grid suspended ceiling: exposed T-bar grid with acoustic or decorative tiles. Standard for commercial fit-outs, offices, retail.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">Key Maidstone ceiling applications:</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">- Maidstone town centre apartment ceilings (often require acoustic treatment for Part E)
